      "key": {
        "uuid": "4fdf57f2_15a6f115",
        "filename": "aom/aom_encoder.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 898,
      "author": {
        "id": 9545
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-27T16:43:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Changing `use_fixed_qp_offsets` to effectively an enum (of values 0, 1, 2) is not ideal because the name \"use_fixed_qp_offsets\" just sounds like a boolean. So I just wanted to confirm with you that this is the simplest API design (ignoring the confusing name).",
      "parentUuid": "65f6128e_c1f7c9d4",
      "revId": "ad380040f9868501de9cdbbd869c7df73d21393f",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ed10f5a4_e688238e",
        "filename": "aom/aom_encoder.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 898,
      "author": {
        "id": 3678645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-27T17:07:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I agree having that the nature of the name doesn\u0027t neatly fit the possible values anymore.\n\nThe current proposal is the simplest API design, in that having no QP offsets is technically a subset of having fixed QP offsets, so introducing such an extension for the encoder option comes intuitively.\n\nAs a precedent: I discovered SVT-AV1 worked in the same way for its equivalent encoder option `use-fixed-qindex-offsets` (0, 1, 2), and I quickly got what I needed because the enum values were documented. So if do the same thing for libaom, I think we should be fine.\n\nWith that said: I\u0027m okay with making this into its own encoder option, if anybody feels strongly about it.",
      "parentUuid": "4fdf57f2_15a6f115",
      "revId": "ad380040f9868501de9cdbbd869c7df73d21393f",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
